        "age13": "Ralf Hütter and Florian Schneider set up Kling Klang, their own studio in Düsseldorf, in 1970, and used it to build custom instruments and write music that rejected American and British rock entirely. It was a deliberate attempt to find a German sound after a war that had made \"German culture\" a loaded phrase.",
        "adult": "Kling Klang, founded in 1970 and run as Kraftwerk's private studio and (from 1975) their own vanity label, let the band work at their own pace outside a commercial label's schedule, which is part of why their catalogue is so tightly controlled and small. The scene around it was less a night-life culture than a studio practice: a search for a distinctly German, post-war electronic identity that avoided the American blues-rock vocabulary most of their contemporaries were still working in."
